Upstream-Issue: https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/116511
Why-upstream-will-not: inlining an image as base64 on every read is free between a local server and a local desktop and is the right default there, so upstream gains nothing by changing it; over a relay the same choice put 105 MiB of base64 on the wire for one session and killed the tunnel, and no remote client decodes it because the image bytes are fetched separately by path
Read-side-only: yes
Added: 2026-09-20

